    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40636" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιπρο-ϊάλλω</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῐ]</span>, poet. Verb, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>set out</i> or <i>place before
				one</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφωΐν ἐπιπροΐηλε τράπεζαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					11.628
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>. <i>send on
				one after another</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεοὺς ἐπιπροΐαλλεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Cer.</u>
					326
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλλον ἐπ᾽</span>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλλῳ ἰόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Q.S.
					6.231
				</span></i>
			.</div>
